I/O Interfaces
==============

There are several standards to communicate from / to a microcontroller.
In the embedded world, the most popular methods are:

- UART: Universal Asynchronous Receiver / Transmitter is one of the
  simplest protocols for communication. It allows two parties to
  communicate via 2 serial lines: RX (receive) and TX (transmit). They
  both need to agree to a baud rate to receive and transmit data
  correctly, it is usually set to 115200 (measured in bits per seconds).
  
- I2C: It allows communication between multiple masters and multiple
  slaves. It uses 2 lines, serial data line (SDA) and serial clock
  line (SCL). The master initiates coommunication and generates the
  clock.

